========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) 9.0.0 - BYPASS HANGS: IDENTIFYING GFS2 MOUNT & MULTIPATH MAPS
========================================================================================================================

1. BYPASS SYSTEM HANGS TO FIND THE GFS2 MOUNT PATH & DEVICE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
cat /proc/mounts | grep gfs2                   Read kernel mount table directly (Will NOT hang like 'df -h')
cat /proc/cluster/services                      Query active DLM kernel layers to view registered storage names
ls -la /sys/fs/gfs2/                            List kernel runtime entries for all active GFS2 filesystems

2. IDENTIFY THE EXACT MULTIPATH MAP NAME & BACKEND SLAVES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
sudo multipath -ll                              Map all redundant paths, disk UUIDs, and active map names
ls -la /dev/mapper/                             List all active logical device mapper paths on the system
dmsetup ls --target multipath                   Query device-mapper framework directly for multipath targets
lsblk -o NAME,TYPE,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINT | grep dm- Trace logical device-mapper tracking IDs back to physical drives

3. VERIFY BLOCK SIZE GEOMETRY SYNCHRONIZATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
sudo blockdev --getsize64 /dev/mapper/<map_id>  Get the raw byte size of the multipath device (Non-blocking)
sudo multipathd show maps status                Check the runtime sync status of all device-mapper maps
